  "extra_findings": [
    "SEC (visibility) — listing returns every ticket to every client (F3, index.php:72-73 / lib.php:78-93); fixed via listarChamadosDoUsuario, which enforces the manifest rule",
    "SEC (visibility) — CSV export returns every ticket to every client (F4, index.php:44-47); fixed via exportarCsvDoUsuario, which filters to the client's own tickets while exportarCsv($db) still exports all",
    "SEC — fixed shared export file EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv: race between concurrent exports and a persistent full dump on disk (F9, lib.php:125-150)",
    "BUG — array-typed login[]/busca[] cause TypeError and HTTP 500 (F16, index.php:22/72)",
    "BUG/SEC — obsolete connect_errno check; uncaught mysqli_sql_exception can leak DB user/host/paths when display_errors is on (F17, index.php:9-12)",
    "SEC — no login rate limiting / brute-force protection (F18, index.php:20-29), reported only",
    "BUG — formatarStatus maps every value other than 1/2 to 'Resolvido' (F20, lib.php:26-35), reported only and deliberately not changed",
    "PERF-002 — SELECT * without LIMIT in listarChamados (F21, lib.php:80-92), reported only",
    "PERF — mediaResposta pulls every row into PHP to sum/count (F13, lib.php:109-115)",
    "CLN — typed-int concatenation in SQL in verChamado/tecnicoNome; the report itself says it is not exploitable today (F22, lib.php:100/69), a hardening finding at confidence 10",
    "SEC — session cookie without HttpOnly/SameSite and use_strict_mode off (bundled in F10, index.php:15)"
